dinput: filter action map app data by device GUID and DIA_APPNOMAP

DirectInput's SetActionMap maps only actions whose guidInstance matches the
target device and whose dwFlags do not set DIA_APPNOMAP. When a program reuses
one DIACTIONFORMAT across multiple devices, such as building and setting an
action map for the keyboard and then for the mouse, unmapped or other-device
actions can retain dwObjID values that match object type IDs on the current
device.

Wine's init_object_app_data matched actions only by dwObjID, so a later
unmapped or other-device entry with a colliding dwObjID overwrote the target
device object's app_data. Skipping DIA_APPNOMAP entries and entries whose
guidInstance differs from the device matches SetActionMap's own filter and
Windows behavior (WINE-IN-4).

--- a/dlls/dinput/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dinput/device.c
@@ -1967,6 +1967,8 @@
 
     while (action-- > format->rgoAction)
     {
+        if (action->dwFlags & DIA_APPNOMAP) continue;
+        if (!IsEqualGUID( &device->guid, &action->guidInstance )) continue;
         if (action->dwObjID != instance->dwType) continue;
         properties->app_data = action->uAppData;
         break;
